{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Set over him a wicked one</b> — after His right hand has prevailed over him, and an adversary stands against him: 'let an enemy prosecute me,' and he is a man, in the manner of 'and YHWH raised up an adversary against Solomon'; likewise 'and he stood,' and he is one of the counselors."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 109, :notes {0 "The comment begins with הפקד רשע, quoting the lemma from Psalms 109:6; rendered as a lemma head."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:11.620709362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}